From 038dab903d3ee943199d6b87830aa53df23b889f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:08:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: queue M4 dependencies in firmware and share
 compute roots

Keep compute save storage in the retained Work allocation, with fresh private
scratch and marker VAs in the persistent VM. Remove CPU CDM/resource reads,
resource snapshots, PTE replacement and per-command page-table forks.

Encode resolved UAPI dependencies as type-1 firmware barriers before TA/CDM.
Account for their ring entries and preserve internal partial-render barriers,
external completion fences and backing ownership through VM destruction.

M4 hardware passes queued mixed partials/TVB growth, 64 computes sharing one
ASID/message/kick, local-indirect GPU geometry and delayed fences/timestamps.
Host ownership, failure, scheduling, batching, notification and wire checks pass.
The mixed replay needs a full caller post-dispatch CDM barrier; qualification
adds it only in the test caller and documents the separate Mesa follow-up.

(cherry picked from commit f6f4ab9555573ee1db0b5f199cd8a252c83a3c69)
